(2. Rate limits) Tj
/F1 11 Tf
15 TL
0 -10 Td
T*
T*
(Each API key may send up to 600 requests per minute. On top of that, short bursts of up) Tj
T*
(to 50 requests in the same second are accepted.) Tj
T*
T*
(When a key goes over its limit, Orbit answers with HTTP status 429 Too Many Requests and) Tj
T*
(a Retry-After header giving the number of seconds to wait. Clients should wait at least) Tj
T*
(that long, then retry with exponential backoff and jitter.) Tj
T*
T*
(Limits are counted per key, not per account: splitting traffic between a reporting key) Tj
T*
(and a checkout key keeps a slow report from blocking payments. Enterprise plans can ask) Tj
T*
(for higher limits.) Tj
ET
BT
